# Cross-plane parity: the ollama-bus lesson store + bash harness must be BYTE-IDENTICAL on every plane so the
# parity-lock token (sha256 of lba-coordinator.Modelfile) matches on Windows and Linux, and so the harness
# scripts stay LF for the bare Linux container. Force LF regardless of a plane's core.autocrlf setting.
experiments/ollama-bus/lba-coordinator.Modelfile text eol=lf
experiments/ollama-bus/*.sh text eol=lf

# Extension-embedded AGENTS.md (issue #98): the manifest pins the file by sha256 over its canonical body, so
# it must stay LF on every plane (a Windows CRLF checkout would otherwise hash differently than the manifest).
extension-agents/AGENTS.md text eol=lf
extension-agents/agents.manifest.json text eol=lf

# Cross-plane .vsix byte-reproducibility (ADR-0067 / LBA-REQ-086): the files packaged into the .vsix -- and the
# experiments/ sources bundled into out/acg-mcp-bundle by stage-acg-mcp -- must be LF on EVERY plane so a Windows
# build and a Linux build of the same commit are byte-identical. *.mjs/*.js/*.md carry no committed CRLF, so LF is
# safe repo-wide; *.json is scoped to the packaged media set to avoid the Windows-captured experiment fixtures
# (experiments/mesh-stress-signature/fixtures/win-vm-*.json are intentionally CRLF and are neither packaged nor bundled).
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
/package.json text eol=lf
/README.md text eol=lf
/CHANGELOG.md text eol=lf
/LICENSE text eol=lf
media/*.json text eol=lf
media/icon.png binary
